window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"graves","b":"locke","win":["Graves","Graves","Graves","Graves","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-4","text":"Peak bully window — point-blank pellets and two True Grit stacks win every trade. Cash it."},{"when":"Enemy 6 + first item","text":"His R executes a squishy Graves — stay off threshold HP and save Quickdraw as the exit."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your item damage matches his execute again — an even fight decided by picks and vision."},{"text":"His R gains additional power for every champion it seals away, so a Locke who has been closing fights carries a bigger execute floor into every next one — deny the seals and the late game he is building never arrives.","when":"Late"}],"wants":{"you":["Chunks on him every wave pre-6","Plates banked from the early lead","HP above execute range after his 6"],"foe":["Survival to 6 without feeding","First-item Purgatory picks","A catch at threshold HP"]},"early":"Levels 1-5 you are simply the bigger bully: double-shell autos and Buckshot out-trade his chip, Smoke Screen blinds his answer mid-pattern, and Quickdraw armor wins the level-3 duel outright. Force a trade every wave and convert into plates — this lead is the whole matchup, because his level 6 rewrites the rules on you.","mid":"From his 6 through first item, respect the flip: Purgatory executes a squishy Graves under threshold, and his burst spike makes one caught rotation lethal. Trade from grass angles at full HP only, keep Quickdraw charged as an exit rather than a poke tool, and spend your early gold lead on the map — you no longer need to beat him in lane.","late":"Two-plus items it is an honest skill fight: your item damage trades evenly against his reliable execute, so discipline decides it. Fight around Smoke Screen and your dash resets, never show below half HP, and use superior waveclear to control picks. End of the Line into a smoke slow wins the exact exchanges he wants to start.","whys":["Level 1 is Graves — four pellets at point-blank out-trade his nail chip openers.","Level 2 stays yours: Smoke Screen's impact slow pins him, and his only exit is a flat 10 seconds.","Level 3 is Graves — dash AT him for two True Grit stacks and win it.","Levels 4-5 stay yours on raw early trading power — keep forcing the exchanges.","Level 6 evens things out — his ult threat now hangs over trades you used to win for free, and your raw-damage lead thins.","First item is Locke's window — Purgatory plus his burst spike executes a squishy Graves caught below threshold; this is the danger stretch.","2+ items returns to skill: your item damage trades evenly against his reliable execute — whoever finds the pick wins."]});
