window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"graves","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Graves","Zaahen","Skill","Graves","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 3","text":"Buckshot-blind-reload DPS window — force the trade before his ult exists."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"His pull and knock-up hunt a spent Quickdraw — hold E as an exit, not a poke tool."},{"when":"First item","text":"Lethality burst beats his sustain — your second big trade window."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"He out-brawls you in long fights — kite, chunk, reset; never stand and trade."}],"wants":{"you":["Forced fights at 3 and first item","Quickdraw held as escape vs his ult","Short burst trades, never brawls"],"foe":["Early-ult all-ins on your spent E","Trades dragged long to out-sustain you","Two-item extended brawls"]},"early":"Open patient — levels 1-2 are pure farming — then hit the gas at 3, where Buckshot, the smoke's sight denial and reload autos out-DPS him point-blank. The catch: his 850-range pull drags you back onto a spent Quickdraw from 4-5 onward, so from that point E is an exit, not a damage tool. Trade hard inside your window, then respect the 4-5 stretch.","mid":"Level 6 balances the ledger — your burst chunks him out of ult commits — and first item tips it back to you: the lethality spike kills through his sustain before it ticks. Look for one-rotation kills off grass angles and smoke he cannot see through. Never let a trade become a brawl: his Q and his R both heal him, and every hit he lands fills Determination.","late":"Two-plus items his extended-fight brawling beats a peel-less Graves, so your rules harden: burst, smoke, Quickdraw out, reset. Every hit he lands fills Determination, and a full bar is bonus AD plus a revive — a long fight literally rebuilds him. If he reaches you at full HP with cooldowns up, that fight was lost before it began — do not take it.","whys":["Level 1 is even — both sides are farming before spells matter.","Level 2 stays even as neither kit is fully online yet.","Level 3 is Graves — Buckshot plus a Smoke Screen that blanks his sight out-damages him up close.","Levels 4-5 are Zaahen's: his 850-range pull drags you back onto a spent Quickdraw — never burn E for damage here.","Level 6 evens out — your burst answers his ult commit, chunking him out of clean all-ins.","First item is Graves: your lethality spike bursts through his sustain before it can matter.","2+ items is Zaahen — a full Determination bar gives him bonus AD and a revive, so never let a fight run long enough to fill it."]});
